    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\ude18Face To Face is a\u00a0satisfying action puzzle game that combines the Physics of Suika Game with a SUPER COOL Set Matching mechanic.\ud83d\ude05 </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udfe6<strong>How to Play\ud83d\udfea</strong> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1. Tap Shapes to give them a face.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2. When faces touch, They kiss and disappear!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >3. Faces can kiss through other objects, as long as each shape has one thing in common with the one before.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(this would be a valid example -&gt; \ud83d\ude18\ud83d\udfe1\ud83d\udfe2\ud83d\udfe9\ud83d\udfe8\ud83d\ude05)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >4. Create longer chains for more points.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udfe6<strong>About the developer\ud83d\udfea</strong>  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Samuel Leigh is a game developer, writer and adjunct professor based in New York. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >His work spans from Interactive fiction, to puzzle and action games. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >His other games, Conversation with a Rock, Annoy this Guy, The Way Down, Blow Out and Moving Jigsaw Puzzles can be played on Steam now!</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\ude18Face To Face is a\u00a0satisfying action puzzle game that combines the Physics of Suika Game with a SUPER COOL Set Matching mechanic.\ud83d\ude05 </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udfe6<strong>How to Play\ud83d\udfea</strong> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1. Tap Shapes to give them a face.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >2. When faces touch, They kiss and disappear!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >3. Faces can kiss through other objects, as long as each shape has one thing in common with the one before.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(this would be a valid example -&gt; \ud83d\ude18\ud83d\udfe1\ud83d\udfe2\ud83d\udfe9\ud83d\udfe8\ud83d\ude05)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >4. Create longer chains for more points.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udfe6<strong>About the developer\ud83d\udfea</strong>  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Samuel Leigh is a game developer, writer and adjunct professor based in New York. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >His work spans from Interactive fiction, to puzzle and action games. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >His other games, Conversation with a Rock, Annoy this Guy, The Way Down, Blow Out and Moving Jigsaw Puzzles can be played on Steam now!</p>",
    "short_description": "\ud83d\ude18A satisfying action puzzle game that merges the physics of Suika Game with a SUPER COOL set-matching mechanic.\ud83d\ude04",
